## Why it happened

Three things lined up. Any one of them alone would likely have limited the damage.

1. A test-environment value was copied into the live settings file. The value, 20, is correct for the test environment but far too small for live traffic.
2. Review did not catch it. The reviewer saw a one-line change and the tool did not show what the live value had been before.
3. There was no gradual rollout, and no easy undo. The change reached every customer at once, and the release system will not undo a change while checkout is unhealthy, which is exactly when an undo is needed.

Detection was also slower than it should be: the alert waits for 5 minutes of sustained failures, so 7 minutes passed before anyone was paged.

### For engineers: the change

```diff
# config/prod/checkout-service.yaml
 database:
-  pool_max_connections: 200
+  pool_max_connections: 20
```

```yaml
# release gate that blocked the rollback
post_deploy_gate:
  require: checkout_success_rate >= 95
  applies_to: [deploy, rollback]
```

## What we are changing

data actions = action,owner,due,status
data actions += Live setting restored to 200 and locked against edits outside the release system,Rafael Mendes,Oct 18,Done
data actions += Page the on-call engineer after 2 minutes of failures instead of 5,Nia Osei,Oct 19,Done
data actions += Show old and new live values side by side in every settings review,Tessa Lindqvist,Oct 23,In progress
data actions += Automatically block any setting that cuts a live limit by more than half unless a second person approves,Tessa Lindqvist,Oct 30,In progress
data actions += Allow an undo even when checkout is unhealthy,Rafael Mendes,Oct 27,In progress
data actions += Roll out settings to 5% of customers first and to everyone after 10 healthy minutes,Jun Park,Nov 13,In progress
data actions += "Email and a $10 credit to the 10,500 customers who did not complete an order",Customer Support,Oct 22,In progress

table actions

! Progress on every action above is reviewed at the Thursday reliability meeting until all are Done.

## Words used in this report

- **Database lines (connection pool):** the fixed number of simultaneous links between checkout and the orders database.
- **Release system:** the tool that delivers code and settings changes to the live site.
- **Rollback (undo):** returning to the previous version of a change.
- **On-call engineer:** the person who is responsible for answering alerts outside office hours.
- **Alert:** an automatic message that tells on-call something is wrong.
